{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788973835,"nonce":"zrklBTh6+APKOCQLToktLcHgUyk=","title":"interact verb: CompInteractable is unreachable, and it is what gates the mech research tree","message":"A third activation surface, and the one currently blocking the run's mech goal. `use` (`d318d4a`) does not reach it: `CompAnalyzable` extends **`CompInteractable`**, not `CompUsable`, and the two have separate gate chains and separate jobs.\n\n## How it was found — openrun-20260909, day 10, live\n\nWith `use` shipped, a `Mechlink` was bought and used, Kimmy became a mechanitor, and `research-set {project:\"BasicMechtech\"}` flipped from `blocked_by:\"mechanitor\"` to `ok:true`. A `TechprofSubpersonaCore` then finished it. The next project stopped the run:\n\n    research-set {project:\"StandardMechtech\"}\n      -\u003e data.ok:false  blocked_by:\"analysis\"  reason:\"requires more analysed items\"\n\nThe whole mech ladder is gated this way, one chip per rung:\n\n| project | cost | requiredAnalyzed |\n|---|---|---|\n| BasicMechtech | 200 | — |\n| StandardMechtech | 1000 | `SignalChip` |\n| HighMechtech | 3000 | `PowerfocusChip` |\n| UltraMechtech | 5000 | `NanostructuringChip` |\n\nAll three chips are **buyable from Dad's catalog on this bench** (500 / 1000 / 1500), so acquisition is solved and analysis is the only blocker. Nothing in the 144 verbs can analyse one.\n\n## The gate to reproduce\n\n`RimWorld/CompAnalyzable : CompInteractable`, with `CompAnalyzableUnlockResearch` as the chip subclass. The precondition is `CompInteractable.CanInteract(Pawn activateBy = null, bool checkOptionalItems = true)`, returning an `AcceptanceReport` — a long chain, each clause its own refusal:\n\n- `Active` -\u003e `AlreadyActive`\n- `OnCooldown` -\u003e `Props.onCooldownString` + remaining duration\n- `refuelable != null \u0026\u0026 !refuelable.HasFuel` -\u003e `Props.outOfFuelMessage ?? NoFuel`\n- `Props.requiresPower \u0026\u0026 power != null \u0026\u0026 !power.PowerOn` -\u003e `NoPower`\n- then, only when `activateBy != null`: `Dead`; `Props.activateStat` disabled for the pawn (**including any `statFactors` disabled for it** — one clause, two tests); `parent.PositionHeld.IsForbidden` and `parent.IsForbidden`, each **skipped when the pawn is drafted or `Props.ignoreForbidden`**, and each naming a different string; `Downed`; `Deathresting`; and more past line 206.\n\n`TryInteract` re-checks with `checkOptionalItems:false` — so **the two calls do not ask the same question** and a verb must not assume one implies the other. `CompInteractable` is also an `ITargetingSource` with `targetParams`, `Targetable =\u003e true` and `MultiSelect =\u003e false`, so some interactables take a target and this overlaps `826d4bf`'s problem.\n\n## Why it is worth its own verb rather than folding into `use`\n\nDifferent comp root, different gate method, different job, different props class (`CompProperties_Interactable` vs `CompProperties_Usable`), and a cooldown/active state model `CompUsable` has no equivalent of. Sharing the *file* with `UsableSafe.cs` is reasonable; sharing the chain is not.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `interact {pawn, thing, target?}` reproduces every `CanInteract` clause under its own gate name, cites file and member, and distinguishes the two forbidden clauses and the drafted/`ignoreForbidden` escapes.\n- `interact-options {pawn?, thing?}` lists interactables with `can_interact`, the gate, the game's reason, `cooldown_ticks_remaining`, `ticks_to_activate`, `requires_power`, `activate_stat`, and whether it is targetable.\n- Buying a `SignalChip` and interacting with it produces the analysis, and `research-set {project:\"StandardMechtech\"}` then answers `data.ok:true`. **That is the end-to-end test and it is the one that matters.**\n- A chip on cooldown, an unpowered interactable, a forbidden one with an undrafted pawn, and a downed pawn each give a distinct named refusal.\n- `checkOptionalItems` is honoured as its own concept, not collapsed into the `TryInteract` re-check.\n- Soft-dependency rules do not apply (this is vanilla), but the `dev:*` split does: `interact` may not bypass a gate.","files":null}]}